Please provide reference information as follows:

AUTHOR NAMES:
 Either {John First and Michael Second} or {First, John and Second, Michael}
 Composite surnames should be put between braces, e.g. {Johannes {von Erste} and Michel {da Silva}}
%

ARTICLE TITLE:
 If there exists a permanent web link for accessing the article online (such as a DOI), the title can be made clickable in the final pdf file, as follows:
 title = {
 \href
 {permalink}
 {article title}
 }
 (see examples below)

 To enforce upper (or lower-) case in article titles, put the desired word between braces, e.g.:
 title = {Interest rates in {Brazil}}
%

WORKING PAPERS, ETC:
 Always check if a working paper has been published in a peer-reviewed journal. If so, use the latter in the references.
%


